      {
        "id": 122654,
        "name": "seesome",
        "username": "seesome",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-11T21:03:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jffdougan\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/48/1882_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jffdougan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Better, make Haka Weyland (Weland/Wayland) Smith.I love the name Ariel thanks to the Tempest, but the Little Mermaid has forever spoiled it for young girls. (Change the&nbsp; pronunciation and it's still OK for Jewish boys.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wayland Smith was my first choice, but I didn't want to go too far down into a Fables comic spiral.</p>\n<p>I know what you mean about Ariel. &nbsp;I used to have a cat named Nemo and everyone thought it was from the Pixar film as opposed to Little Nemo in Slumberland (his actual namesake).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
