        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"seesome\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/48/2018_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> seesome:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>jffdougan wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Better, make Haka Weyland (Weland/Wayland) Smith.I love the name Ariel thanks to the Tempest, but the Little Mermaid has forever spoiled it for young girls. (Change the&nbsp; pronunciation and it's still OK for Jewish boys.)\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWayland Smith was my first choice, but I didn't want to go too far down into a Fables comic spiral.I know what you mean about Ariel. &nbsp;I used to have a cat named Nemo and everyone thought it was from the Pixar film as opposed to Little Nemo in Slumberland (his actual namesake).&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>See, I don't think Fables. My first introduction to Wayland Smith was Susan Cooper's Dark is rising books.</p>",
